{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"religious-freakish-muskox","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## The problem\n\nThree bot alert lanes close their own alert tickets with an automated `--force=<reason>` —\nthe same gate bypass `AGENTS.md` forbids agents from using and reserves for a human\njudgement call:\n\n- `scripts/dependency_audit.py` `cmd_advisory_alert` (dependency advisories)\n- `scripts/canary_bridge.py` `cmd_heartbeat_alert` (reconcile-bridge heartbeat)\n- `scripts/canary_bridge.py` `cmd_binding_drift_alert` (bridge fsck drift)\n\nEach carries the same stated justification: \"bot alert tickets have no completion\ncriteria to verify\". That justification is accurate — these tickets record an external\ncondition, not a unit of work — but the conclusion drawn from it is wrong. \"This ticket\nclass has nothing to verify\" is an argument for a **disposition path** for such tickets,\nnot for automating the override that exists for human judgement.\n\nDiscovered while fixing `7147-6ea7-90b4-44b1` (`wooded-timid-gallinule`), whose third\nacceptance criterion states this directly: *\"If advisory tickets genuinely have no\ncompletion criteria to verify, that is an argument for giving them a disposition path,\nnot for automating the override that exists for human judgement.\"* That ticket narrows\nthe blast radius — it makes the force-close **unreachable when the audit produced no\nverdict**, which was the security defect — but leaves the override itself in place on\nthe genuine-clear path.\n\n## Why it was not fixed there\n\n- `require_completion_verification_for_close = true` in `rebar.toml`. Dropping `--force`\n  with no replacement route would leave every bot alert lane unable to close the ticket\n  it filed — trading a latent failure for a certain one, on three lanes at once.\n- `tests/scripts/test_dependency_audit.py::test_advisory_alert_close_argv_survives_the_real_transition_parser`\n  (ticket `24f7`) currently ASSERTS a force reason reaches the real `transition` parser,\n  so the flag is pinned by an existing regression test that would have to move with it.\n- The fix is a rebar-core change, not a CI-script change: it needs a sanctioned close\n  route for tickets with no completion criteria. That is new mechanism (mechanism-delta\n  ratchet) and plausibly ADR territory.\n\n## Sketch of the shape (not a decision)\n\nOptions to weigh, in the ADR:\n\n1. A **close class** for externally-observed conditions that the completion gate treats\n   as certifiable-by-construction (the condition itself is the criterion).\n2. A **ticket type** (or tag) for bot alerts whose close gate is the alerting oracle's\n   own verdict rather than a completion verifier.\n3. A **detected-by-scoped** disposition: a ticket filed by `--detected-by <lane>` may be\n   closed by that same lane without a bypass, recording the lane as the attestor.\n\nWhichever is chosen must leave a durable audit signal at least as strong as today's\n\"absent attestation\" signal, and must apply to all three lanes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] An ADR records the chosen disposition route for tickets with no completion\n      criteria, and why it is preferred over the other options sketched above.\n- [ ] `cmd_advisory_alert` closes its ticket without `--force`.\n- [ ] `cmd_heartbeat_alert` closes its ticket without `--force`.\n- [ ] `cmd_binding_drift_alert` closes its ticket without `--force`.\n- [ ] The 24f7 regression test is updated to pin the NEW close route through the real\n      `rebar transition` parser (not deleted).\n- [ ] A test proves a bot alert close is refused when the ticket is NOT a bot alert\n      ticket, so the new route is not a general-purpose bypass.","id":"81e1-63a4-91ea-4974","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Bot alert lanes force-close their own tickets: give no-completion-criteria tickets a disposition path instead of an automated --force"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788586590098042001,"uuid":"e1163728-c931-4aa8-b2e5-944d397debde"}